Chapter: BrotliDictTest
  cites Compress chapter BrotliDict
  cites Compress chapter BrotliDictIndex
  cites Compress chapter Brotli

 The RFC 7932 corpus survives the trip into Codex source and back out.

 THE SIZE ALONE PROVES NOTHING. A corpus of the right length with the wrong
 bytes in it is exactly the failure this chapter exists to catch, and it is the
 one failure our own round-trip can never see: the encoder and the decoder would
 look the word up in the same wrong copy and agree with each other perfectly. So
 the pin is a SUM over every byte as well as a length, and four words read out at
 known offsets -- the first two four-byte words, the first six-byte word, and the
 first of the longest length, which sits at the far end of the corpus and is what
 a walk that ran short would miss.

 The words are pinned as BYTES, not as text. Comparing rendered text would put
 the CCE boundary in the middle of the assertion, and a word full of punctuation
 (&quot; and a script tag are two of the four) is exactly where that conversion
 is least trustworthy. These are the bytes a decoder copies; they are what the
 test should be about.

 We say:

Section: Helpers

  sum-bytes : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sum-bytes (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else sum-bytes xs (i + 1) n (acc + list-at xs i)

 The counts multiplied by their own lengths. If the walk stopped early at any
 length this does not reach 122784.

  counts-bytes : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  counts-bytes (len) (acc) =
    if len > brdict-max-len then acc
    else counts-bytes (len + 1) (acc + brdict-count len * len)

  bytes-equal : List Integer, Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bytes-equal (d) (off) (want) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then True
    else if list-at d (off + i) == list-at want i then bytes-equal d off want (i + 1) n
    else False

  say : Text, Integer, Integer -> Text
  say (label) (got) (want) =
    label & "=" & if got == want then "pass" else "fail(" & show got & ")"

  say-word : Text, List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> Text
  say-word (label) (d) (len) (idx) (want) =
    label & "=" & if bytes-equal d (brdict-word-at len idx) want 0 len then "pass" else "fail"

Section: Body

  want-w4-0 : List Integer = [116, 105, 109, 101]
  want-w4-1 : List Integer = [100, 111, 119, 110]
  want-w6-0 : List Integer = [38, 113, 117, 111, 116, 59]
  want-w24-0 : List Integer = [60, 115, 99, 114, 105, 112, 116, 32, 116, 121, 112, 101, 61, 34, 116, 101, 120, 116, 47, 106, 97, 118, 97, 115]

 One load, threaded into every check. Every reference to a list constant rebuilds
 it, so loading per check would allocate a megabyte eight times over.

 THE TRANSFORM DECODER HAS NOTHING OF OURS TO EXERCISE IT: our encoder emits
 transform zero and nothing else, so a round-trip cannot reach the other 120. The
 streams below were therefore built by an INDEPENDENT implementation
 (build/brotli-xform-cases.ps1) and the bytes each must decode to are what .NET
 decodes them to. That makes this a comparison against the oracle rather than
 against ourselves, which is the only kind that can fail here.

 The last case is the one worth keeping. RFC 7932's case transform is defined on
 UTF-8 BYTES: a two-byte character has bit 5 of its SECOND byte flipped, not its
 first. That word goes 216,177,... to 216,145,... -- and a decoder that upper-cased
 by character instead of by byte would leave it untouched and pass every ASCII
 case above.

  xs-suffix-space : List Integer = [130, 0, 0, 0, 4, 64, 8, 18, 32, 1]
  want-suffix-space : List Integer = [116, 105, 109, 101, 32]
  xs-ferment-first : List Integer = [98, 0, 0, 0, 4, 64, 8, 18, 38, 1, 1]
  want-ferment-first : List Integer = [84, 105, 109, 101]
  xs-suffix-the : List Integer = [2, 1, 0, 0, 4, 64, 8, 18, 36, 1, 1]
  want-suffix-the : List Integer = [116, 105, 109, 101, 32, 116, 104, 101, 32]
  xs-ferment-all : List Integer = [162, 0, 0, 0, 4, 64, 16, 18, 44, 1, 24]
  want-ferment-all : List Integer = [38, 81, 85, 79, 84, 59]
  xs-ferment-utf8 : List Integer = [162, 0, 0, 0, 4, 64, 16, 18, 232, 157, 2]
  want-ferment-utf8 : List Integer = [216, 145, 216, 175, 217, 136]

  same-bytes : List Integer, List Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  same-bytes (a) (b) (i) =
    if i >= list-length a then True
    else if list-at a i == list-at b i then same-bytes a b (i + 1)
    else False

  say-decode : Text, List Integer, List Integer -> Text
  say-decode (label) (stream) (want) =
    let got = brotli-decompress stream
    in label & "=" & if list-length got == list-length want then
         (if same-bytes want got 0 then "pass" else "fail(bytes)")
       else "fail(len " & show (list-length got) & ")"
  report : List Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  report (d) = act
    print-line-uni (say "dict-total" (list-length d) brdict-total)
    print-line-uni (say "dict-words" brdict-words 13504)
    print-line-uni (say "dict-counts-multiply" (counts-bytes brdict-min-len 0) brdict-total)
    print-line-uni (say "dict-sum" (sum-bytes d 0 brdict-total 0) 14054652)
    print-line-uni (say-word "dict-w4-0" d 4 0 want-w4-0)
    print-line-uni (say-word "dict-w4-1" d 4 1 want-w4-1)
    print-line-uni (say-word "dict-w6-0" d 6 0 want-w6-0)
    print-line-uni (say-word "dict-w24-0" d 24 0 want-w24-0)
  end

  probe-hit : List Integer = [120, 120, 112, 111, 115, 105, 116, 105, 111, 110, 121, 121]
  probe-miss : List Integer = [120, 120, 122, 113, 106, 118, 119, 107, 120, 122, 121, 121]

  report-index : BrDictIx -> [Console] Nothing
  report-index (ix) = act
    print-line-uni (say "dict-index-slots" (ix.bx-n) brdict-words)
    print-line-uni (say "dict-find-len" (brdix-slot-len ix (brdix-find ix probe-hit 2 8)) 8)
    print-line-uni (say "dict-find-idx" (brdix-slot-idx ix (brdix-find ix probe-hit 2 8)) 0)
    print-line-uni (say "dict-find-miss" (brdix-find ix probe-miss 2 8) (0 - 1))
    print-line-uni (say "dict-find-short" (brdix-find ix probe-hit 2 5) (0 - 1))
  end

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    report (brdict-load 0)
    report-index (brdix-build (brdict-load 0))
    print-line-uni (say-decode "xf-suffix-space" xs-suffix-space want-suffix-space)
    print-line-uni (say-decode "xf-ferment-first" xs-ferment-first want-ferment-first)
    print-line-uni (say-decode "xf-suffix-the" xs-suffix-the want-suffix-the)
    print-line-uni (say-decode "xf-ferment-all" xs-ferment-all want-ferment-all)
    print-line-uni (say-decode "xf-ferment-utf8" xs-ferment-utf8 want-ferment-utf8)
  end
